# Esc-Esc on an empty, idle input opens the Rewind dialog
# (internal/tui/dialog_rewind.go, wired by app.go's openRewind /
# keys.go's double-Esc Router). Two completed turns give it real history:
# navigate to the older one and confirm the transcript truncates to just
# before it. Esc-to-cancel is covered separately in
# rewind-empty-input-esc.steps.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/dialogs-rewind.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE run this shell command and report its output: echo turn-one
KEY enter
WAITFOR /First turn reply from kiln/ 20
SHOT turn-one
TYPE run this shell command and report its output: echo turn-two
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Second turn reply from kiln/ 20
SHOT turn-two
KEY esc esc
WAITFOR /Restore the code and\/or conversation to the point before/ 20
SHOT rewind-dialog-open
EXPECT /Rewind/
EXPECT /run this shell command and report its output: echo turn-one/
EXPECT /run this shell command and report its output: echo turn-two/
EXPECT /\(current\)/
KEY up
SHOT rewind-navigated
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Rewound to before: run this shell command and report its output: echo turn-two/ 20
SHOT rewind-applied
EXPECT /Rewound to before: run this shell command and report its output: echo turn-two/
EXPECT /First turn reply from kiln/
EXPECT_NOT /Second turn reply from kiln/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
